CodeBrix patch 0010 - opt-in IEEE floating point for WGSL compiled to Metal
(wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs, wgpu-hal/src/metal/device.rs)

WHAT: a process-wide switch, wgpu_hal::metal::CODEBRIX_PRECISE_MATH (off by default), read where the
Metal backend compiles naga's MSL for a pipeline stage (Device::load_shader). When it is on, the
MTLCompileOptions get mathMode = MTLMathModeSafe and mathFloatingPointFunctions =
MTLMathFloatingPointFunctionsPrecise (macOS 15 / iOS 18 and later), or fastMathEnabled = NO before
those systems. codebrix-wgpu's wgpuCodebrixSetMetalPreciseMath sets it (specs/codebrix.yml).
Passthrough MSL (ShaderInput::Msl / Metallib) is never changed. With the switch off, nothing differs
from the unpatched crate.
WHY: wgpu-hal sets only the language version and preserveInvariance, so every WGSL kernel compiles
with Metal's default fast math. Measured on an Intel UHD 630 (macOS 15.8, 2026-10-26, through this
library's osx-x64 build): `x != x` is false for a NaN (NaN checks are removed), the error term of an
error-free sum folds to 0 (reassociation), sin/cos are 80/29 ulps from the correctly rounded value.
WGSL's accuracy rules allow that, so the default stays; a consumer whose kernels depend on IEEE
behaviour (CodeBrix.Graphics3D.Cycles' WGSL device) opts in. Neither setting stops the Metal
compiler from contracting a*b+c into an FMA (measured: still fused).
UPSTREAM: wgpu 29.0.3 has no option for this. CodeBrix's own change. wgpu-hal is vendored for it
(wgpu-hal/, the unmodified crates.io archive; UPSTREAM.txt) and replaces the crates.io crate
through [patch.crates-io] in codebrix-wgpu/Cargo.toml.

--- a/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs
+++ b/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs
@@ -26,6 +26,14 @@
 mod surface;
 mod time;
 
+/// CodeBrix (patches/0010): when `true`, every WGSL shader this process compiles to MSL is compiled
+/// with IEEE floating-point semantics (`MTLMathMode::Safe` and precise math functions; on systems
+/// before macOS 15 / iOS 18, fast math disabled) instead of Metal's default fast math, which lets
+/// the compiler assume no NaN or infinity, reassociate and use approximate transcendental functions.
+/// Process-wide, off by default, read when each pipeline's shader is compiled; set by
+/// `wgpuCodebrixSetMetalPreciseMath`. Passthrough MSL is never affected.
+pub static CODEBRIX_PRECISE_MATH: atomic::AtomicBool = atomic::AtomicBool::new(false);
+
 use alloc::{
     string::{String, ToString as _},
     sync::Arc,
--- a/wgpu-hal/src/metal/device.rs
+++ b/wgpu-hal/src/metal/device.rs
@@ -232,6 +232,19 @@
                     options.setPreserveInvariance(true);
                 }
 
+                // CodeBrix (patches/0010): opt-in IEEE floating point (super::CODEBRIX_PRECISE_MATH).
+                if super::CODEBRIX_PRECISE_MATH.load(atomic::Ordering::Relaxed) {
+                    if available!(macos = 15.0, ios = 18.0, tvos = 18.0, visionos = 2.0) {
+                        options.setMathMode(objc2_metal::MTLMathMode::Safe);
+                        options.setMathFloatingPointFunctions(
+                            objc2_metal::MTLMathFloatingPointFunctions::Precise,
+                        );
+                    } else {
+                        #[allow(deprecated)]
+                        options.setFastMathEnabled(false);
+                    }
+                }
+
                 let library = self
                     .shared
                     .device
